      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4806_Start5" name="Bulky BOPIS order (lumber/tile/appliance per profile §6.2); refrigerated/sensitive item">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4806_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4806_Task6" name="For oversize/bulky orders (lumber packs, cement/tile, appliances, furniture)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: For oversize/bulky orders (lumber packs, cement/tile, appliances, furniture), determine locker-eligibility vs counter/curbside (W4758-style) fallback: only assign if an oversize compartment fits and is safe to self-collect; otherwise route to counter/curbside pickup (VS-10) or delivery (VS-06.3)
Responsible (R): OMS / Store Ops / Locker Platform
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager
Duration: Per order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4806_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4806_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4806_Task7" name="For refrigerated/temperature-sensitive items (if offered — e.g., certain…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: For refrigerated/temperature-sensitive items (if offered — e.g., certain garden/live-adjacent or specialty), use refrigerated locker compartments, manage the temperature monitoring (VS-138 BMS, VS-145 live-goods pattern), the shorter hold-period, and the spoilage/disposition if uncollected (VS-05.3)
Responsible (R): Store Ops / Facilities / Locker Program
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager / Store Manager
Duration: Per order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4806_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4806_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4806_Task8" name="Communicate clearly to the customer: oversize handling (e.g., forklift/assist…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Communicate clearly to the customer: oversize handling (e.g., forklift/assist at pickup vs self-service), refrigerated-item urgency, and any safety/weight notes; manage the customer-experience distinct from standard locker pickup (W4805)
Responsible (R): CX / Store Ops
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager / Store Manager
Duration: Per order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4806_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4806_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4806_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4806_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
