    <bpmn:process id="W_W4808" name="W4808. Daily Locker Reconciliation, Inventory Accuracy &amp; Exception Handling" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily close (VS-07); inventory cycle (VS-05); exception alert
Frequency: Daily + per exception
Volume: ~daily recon across all locker banks
Owner: Locker Program Manager / Store Ops (VS-07) / Finance
Participants: Store Ops (VS-07), Inventory (VS-05), IT (VS-27), LP (VS-23)
Source: workflow W4808 — Daily Locker Reconciliation, Inventory Accuracy &amp; Exception Handling</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4808_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4808_Lane1" name="Store Ops">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4808_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4808_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4808_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4808_Lane2" name="Analytics">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4808_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4808_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4808_Start4" name="Daily close (VS-07); inventory cycle (VS-05); exception alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4808_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4808_Task5" name="Reconcile daily: physical compartment state (occupied/empty) vs locker-platform…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Reconcile daily: physical compartment state (occupied/empty) vs locker-platform state vs OMS/inventory state (VS-10/VS-05); investigate variances (phantom-occupied, phantom-empty, missing item) and resolve to maintain ≥97% inventory-accuracy target (profile §6.3)
Responsible (R): Store Ops / Inventory / IT
Accountable (A): Store Manager / Locker Program Manager
Duration: Daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4808_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4808_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4808_Task6" name="Handle exceptions: stuck-locked compartment, failed-open, sensor fault…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Handle exceptions: stuck-locked compartment, failed-open, sensor fault, mis-pick, item-not-found, suspected theft (VS-23) — with documented triage and resolution; manage the customer impact (refund/replacement per VS-101/VS-32) for any loss
Responsible (R): Store Ops / IT / LP / CX
Accountable (A): Store Manager / LP
Duration: Per exception</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4808_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4808_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4808_Task7" name="Feed variance/exception data to analytics (W4815), inventory accuracy (VS-05)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Feed variance/exception data to analytics (W4815), inventory accuracy (VS-05), and LP/theft investigation (VS-23); drive root-cause improvement (VS-133) on recurring exceptions
Responsible (R): Analytics / Inventory / LP / Locker Program
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager
Duration: Daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4808_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4808_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4808_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4808_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4808_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-95 (ensure locker network custody &amp; uptime.) | - CTL-723: daily recon to ≥97% accuracy; exceptions triaged &amp; resolved; variances investigated (LP VS-23); root-cause fed to improvement
Owner: Locker Program Manager / Store Ops (VS-07) / Finance</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
